        <div class="container-fluid">
            <div >
                


<div class="component container col-12">
    <div class="component-content" >

    <div class="component footnotes col-12">
        <div class="component-content">
<div class="cf-footnotes">
    <h5>Footnotes</h5>
        <ol>
                    <li id="cf-fn-1">Stephanie Aaronson, Tomaz Cajner, Bruce Fallick, Felix Galbis-Reig, Christopher L. Smith, and William Wascher,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://www.federalreserve.gov/pubs/feds/2014/201464/201464pap.pdf">&ldquo;Labor Force Participation: Recent Developments and Future Prospects,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;Finance and Economics Discussion Series Paper 2014-64, Federal Reserve Board, September 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-1" aria-label="Return from footnote 1.">Return to 1</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-2">See Loretta J. Mester and Guhan Venkatu,&nbsp;<a href="/collections/mester-works/lm002-job-quality-during-the-expansion">&ldquo;Job Quality During the Expansion,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;manuscript, March 2015. The same type of pattern holds in the four states in the Cleveland Federal Reserve District: Ohio, Pennsylvania, Kentucky, and West Virginia.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-2" aria-label="Return from footnote 2.">Return to 2</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-3">Brent Meyer, Guhan Venkatu, and Saeed Zaman,&nbsp;<a href="/publications/economic-commentary/2013/ec-201305-forecasting-inflation-target-the-middle">&ldquo;Forecasting Inflation? Target the Middle,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland&nbsp;<em>Economic Commentary</em>, April 2013.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-3" aria-label="Return from footnote 3.">Return to 3</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-4">See Jon Faust and Jonathan H. Wright,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://books.google.com/books?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;id=-_dSuakNHWYC&amp;oi=fnd&amp;pg=PA3&amp;dq=faust+Forecasting+Inflation,%E2%80%9D+Handbook+of+Economic+Forecasting&amp;ots=4lF3t6m7wF&amp;sig=V7vtSrycDvuABZ4Mfz3R22BRj34#v=onepage&amp;q=faust%20Forecasting%20Inflation%2C%E2%80%9D%20Handbook%20of%20Economic%20Forecasting&amp;f=false">&ldquo;Forecasting Inflation,&rdquo;</a> <em>Handbook of Economic Forecasting</em>, 2A, Graham Elliott and Allan Timmermann, eds., New York: Elsevier, pp. 3-56, and Todd E. Clark and Taeyoung Doh,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/intfor/v30y2014i3p426-448.html">&ldquo;Evaluating Alternative Models of Trend Inflation,&rdquo;</a> <em>International Journal of Forecasting</em>, 30(3), 2014, pp. 426-448.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-4" aria-label="Return from footnote 4.">Return to 4</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-5">Randal Verbrugge and Amy Higgins, &ldquo;Do Energy Prices Drive the Long-Term Inflation Expectations of Households?&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland <em>Economic Trends</em>, March 24, 2015.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-5" aria-label="Return from footnote 5.">Return to 5</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-6">See Loretta J. Mester, &ldquo;The Nexus of Macroprudential Supervision, Monetary Policy, and Financial Stability,&rdquo; remarks at the Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland and the Office of Financial Research 2014 Financial Stability Conference: &ldquo;Measurement Challenges in Macroprudential Policy Implementation: Essential Data Elements for Preserving Financial Stability,&rdquo; Washington DC, December 5, 2014.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-6" aria-label="Return from footnote 6.">Return to 6</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-7">For a discussion, see John B. Taylor, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://object.cato.org/sites/cato.org/files/serials/files/cato-journal/2013/9/cjv33n3-2.pdf">&ldquo;Monetary Policy During the Past 30 Years with Lessons for the Next 30 Years,&rdquo;</a> luncheon address at the Cato Institute&rsquo;s 30th Annual Monetary Conference on Money, Markets and Government: The Next 30 Years, Washington DC, November 15, 2012.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-7" aria-label="Return from footnote 7.">Return to 7</a>
                    </li>
        </ol>
</div>
